### ─── AUTHORIZATION & SCOPED TOKENS ──────────────────────────────────────────
###
### MoltenDB uses a single root user. The root user delegates narrow-permission
### JWTs to clients via POST /auth/delegate. Clients never see the root password.
###
### Scope format:  action:collection:document_key
###   action       →  read | write | delete
###   collection   →  exact name, or * for any collection
###   document_key →  exact key
###                   * for any document in the collection
###                   prefix* for any key starting with prefix (e.g. store_A_*)
###   *:*:*        →  special scope granting full access to everything
###
### SCOPE → ENDPOINT COMPATIBILITY
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  Scope                        │ /get │ /collections/:c/docs/:k │ /set │ /update │ /delete │ /snapshot
###  ─────────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────────────────────┼──────┼─────────┼─────────┼──────────
###  read:laptops:lp1             │ lp1  │ ✅ lp1 only              │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:lp1,lp2         │lp1+2 │ ✅ lp1 or lp2           │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:store_A_*       │store_A_*│ ✅ store_A_* keys only │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:*               │  ✅  │ ✅ any key               │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  write:laptops:*              │  ❌  │ ❌                       │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  delete:laptops:*             │  ❌  │ ❌                       │  ❌  │   ❌    │   ✅    │    ❌
###  read:laptops:* + write:*     │  ✅  │ ✅                       │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  read:*:* + write:*:*         │  ✅  │ ✅ any col/key           │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ❌    │    ❌
###  *:*:*                        │  ✅  │ ✅                       │  ✅  │   ✅    │   ✅    │    ✅
###
### HOW TO USE THESE EXAMPLES
###   1. Make sure you have a valid root token in @token (see §1 at the top).
###   2. Run a "Mint" request below to get a scoped token.
###   3. Copy the returned token value into the matching @variable.
###   4. Run the usage examples with that variable.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LEVEL 1 — DOCUMENT-LEVEL READ (narrowest possible access)
### Scopes: read:laptops:lp1, read:laptops:lp2
###
### This token can only read two specific documents. It cannot query the
### collection, write, delete, or access any other document.
### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Mint — document-level read token
POST http://localhost:1538/auth/delegate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "client_id": "field-rep",
  "scopes": ["read:laptops:lp1", "read:laptops:lp2"],
  "ttl_secs": 3600
}

###

@doc_token = eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJmaWVsZC1yZXAiLCJleHAiOjE3Nzc1Njg2MjksInNjb3BlcyI6WyJyZWFkOmxhcHRvcHM6bHAxIiwicmVhZDpsYXB0b3BzOmxwMiJdLCJqdGkiOiJlOGFkMzM4NS1lNDhkLTQ1ZmQtOGUwNi00N2Y5MTRlM2IzOGYifQ.Vo-IzSDCWFkGEbYcnn4xzITPVa4qJP4HGqn794HAvNo

### ✅ Fetch lp1 — in scope
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/lp1
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

###

### ✅ Fetch lp2 — in scope
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/lp2
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

###

### ❌ Fetch lp3 — not in scopes → 403 Forbidden
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/lp3
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

###

### ✅ POST /get without keys — server automatically returns only lp1 + lp2
### No other documents are returned, even if the collection has hundreds.
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"]
}

###

### ✅ POST /get with explicit allowed key — lp2 is in scope
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp2",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"]
}

###

### ❌ POST /get with a key not in scope → 403 Forbidden
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "keys": "lp99"
}

###

### ❌ POST /set — write not granted → 403 Forbidden
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{doc_token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "lp1": { "brand": "Hacked", "model": "Nope", "price": 0, "in_stock": false }
  }
}

###


### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### LEVEL 1.5 — PREFIX-WILDCARD READ (store/tenant-scoped access)
### Scopes: read:laptops:store_A_*
###
### This token can only read documents whose key starts with "store_A_".
### It cannot read other documents, write, delete, or query the full collection.
### POST /get with no keys returns only the matching documents (server-side filtered).
### ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Mint — prefix-wildcard read token
POST http://localhost:1538/auth/delegate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "client_id": "store-a-rep",
  "scopes": ["read:laptops:store_A_*"],
  "ttl_secs": 3600
}

###

@prefix_token = eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJzdG9yZS1hLXJlcCIsImV4cCI6MTc3NzU1NDI3Niwic2NvcGVzIjpbInJlYWQ6bGFwdG9wczpzdG9yZV9BXyoiXX0.k6rjtf3C0MkBMkm2Yy7QWlUplxRyL0aJRYQMa24WZek

### ✅ Fetch a document whose key starts with store_A_ (allowed)
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/store_A_001
Authorization: Bearer {{prefix_token}}

###

### ❌ Fetch a document outside the prefix → 403 Forbidden
GET http://localhost:1538/collections/laptops/docs/lp1
Authorization: Bearer {{prefix_token}}

###

### ✅ POST /get — no keys specified: returns only store_A_* documents
POST http://localhost:1538/get
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{prefix_token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "fields": ["brand", "model", "price"]
}

###

### ❌ POST /set — write not granted → 403 Forbidden
POST http://localhost:1538/set
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{prefix_token}}

{
  "collection": "laptops",
  "data": {
    "store_A_999": { "brand": "Hacked", "model": "Nope", "price": 0, "in_stock": false }
  }
}

